Malaga Event Gear (MEG) is a single trade audio visual rental company, so choosing wedding rentals from us is narrower than most guides make it sound: the whole catalog for a wedding is two packages, not a hundred categories of furniture, decor and tableware. This page is a short decision framework that walks through what actually decides which package fits your day, then points to the guide that covers each question in depth rather than repeating it here. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

Six questions decide which wedding AV rental fits your day, roughly in order: guest count, indoor or outdoor venue, whether the venue already has a house sound system, whether you want a technician managing the sound, what moves the price, and how early to book. Answer the first one and you already know whether the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) or the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is the right starting point. The rest refine that choice or point you to a guide with more depth than this page needs.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Guest count is the first filter: up to 50 guests points to the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), up to 80 points to the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/).
-   Indoor and outdoor venues raise different AV questions, room acoustics against wind and curfews, each covered in its own guide rather than repeated here.
-   A house sound system at your venue rarely replaces what a wedding AV rental actually needs, and our cost guide covers exactly why.
-   Wanting a technician on site is really the Eco Pack versus Wedding Pack question restated, not a separate decision.
-   Vetting the specific provider you choose, once you know which package fits, is its own separate step with its own guide.

<InlineCTA />

## Step 1: Guest Count Decides the Package First

Start here, before venue type or budget. MEG's wedding catalog has exactly two packages, sized by guest count.

| | Eco Pack | Wedding Pack |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guest count | Up to 50 | Up to 80 |
| Technician on site | No, self run after setup | Yes, throughout the event |
| Lighting | RGBW LED spotlights | Fairy lights and warm LED strings |
| Price (ex VAT) | 290 euros | 650 euros |

If your guest list is under 50, the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is very likely your answer already. Between 50 and 80, the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is the only one that covers you. Over 80, [contact us](/contact/) directly rather than assuming either package scales up.

## Step 2: Indoor or Outdoor Venue

Once guest count narrows the package, venue type shapes how it gets set up. An indoor room and an open air finca or beach raise genuinely different AV questions, room acoustics against wind, curfews and power, each with enough depth to deserve its own guide. Read our [indoor wedding rental essentials](/blog/indoor-wedding-rental-essentials/) guide for a ballroom or hall, or our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide for a finca, villa or beach ceremony.

## Step 3: Does Your Venue Already Have a House PA?

Before renting anything, from us or anyone else, ask your venue whether it already has a sound system built in. Some fincas, hotels and villas around Malaga do. Whether that changes what you still need to rent is covered in full in our [tips for reducing wedding rental costs](/blog/tips-for-reducing-wedding-rental-costs/) guide.

## Step 4: Do You Actually Need a Technician?

This is the guest count question from Step 1, asked a different way. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is delivered, installed and tested by our crew, then left running unattended. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) includes a live technician who stays through vows, speeches and dancing. If a hands off setup is fine for your day, the Eco Pack's guest count ceiling is the only real constraint. If you want someone managing sound as the day unfolds, that pushes you toward the Wedding Pack even at a count the Eco Pack could technically cover.

## Step 5: What Actually Moves the Price

Right sizing your package to guest count, from Step 1, is the single biggest real cost lever. Add ons, negotiation and the Granada distance threshold are covered in full in our [tips for reducing wedding rental costs](/blog/tips-for-reducing-wedding-rental-costs/) guide.

## Step 6: Vetting the Provider You Choose

Once you know which package fits, the next step is vetting the company you book it from, whether that is MEG or someone else. What is included, whether a technician is on site, how many guests the system covers, and whether VAT is already in the price are the four questions worth asking any provider, covered in full in our [questions to ask a wedding rental company](/blog/questions-to-ask-wedding-rental-companies/) guide.

## Step 7: When to Book

There is no fixed lead time, only availability, and dates and technicians fill up fastest in peak season. See our [booking timeline](/blog/timeline-for-booking-wedding-rentals/) guide for how to plan around that once your venue and date are set.

